# 🪙 Bitcoin UTXO Viewer — Complete Project Explanation

## 1. What Is This Project? (In Simple Terms)

Imagine you have a Bitcoin wallet. Your "balance" is actually made up of many small pieces of Bitcoin — like having a wallet full of different denomination coins instead of one single bill. Each of those pieces is called a **UTXO** (Unspent Transaction Output).

This project is a **full-stack web app** that:
1. **Shows** you all the UTXOs of any Bitcoin address
2. **Analyzes** how healthy your wallet is (too many tiny UTXOs = bad)
3. **Estimates fees** for sending Bitcoin
4. **Optimizes** which UTXOs to pick when you want to send a specific amount

> **View-only** — it never touches your private keys. It only reads publicly available blockchain data.

---

## 2. What Problem Does It Solve?

| Problem | How This App Solves It |
|---|---|
| "How much Bitcoin does this address have?" | Fetches and shows all UTXOs with real-time balances |
| "My wallet has hundreds of tiny UTXOs — is that a problem?" | **Fragmentation Score** shows how fragmented your wallet is (0–100) |
| "How much will it cost to send 0.1 BTC right now?" | **Live fee estimator** shows High/Medium/Low priority costs |
| "Which UTXOs should I pick to minimize fees when sending?" | **Smart Coin Selection** runs two algorithms and picks the cheapest |
| "What are dust outputs in my wallet?" | Flags any UTXO < 546 satoshis as "Dust" (unusable in practice) |

---

