## 11. Key Bitcoin Concepts Used in This App

| Term | Meaning in This App |
|---|---|
| **UTXO** | "Unspent Transaction Output" — a piece of Bitcoin you received and haven't spent yet |
| **Satoshi (sat)** | Smallest Bitcoin unit. 1 BTC = 100,000,000 satoshis |
| **Dust** | UTXOs < 546 sat — so small the fee to spend them exceeds their value |
| **Confirmations** | How many blocks have been mined since the tx was included. More = safer |
| **Block Height** | The sequential number of the block containing this transaction |
| **scriptType** | P2PKH/P2SH/P2WPKH/P2TR — different Bitcoin address/script formats |
| **fee rate (sat/vB)** | Satoshis per virtual byte — how fast your transaction gets confirmed |
| **coin selection** | Choosing WHICH UTXOs to use as inputs for a new transaction |
| **fragmentation** | Having many small UTXOs — costs more in fees to spend later |
| **Taproot (P2TR)** | Newest Bitcoin address format starting with `bc1p` |
